# {{appName}}

{{#if sdi}}A single-document (SDI) desktop application{{/if}}{{#if mdi}}A multiple-document (MDI) desktop application{{/if}}{{#if dialog}}A dialog-based desktop application{{/if}}{{#if outlook}}An Outlook-style desktop application{{/if}} built with RapidSwing on Java 8.

## Build and run

RapidSwing {{rapidswingVersion}} must be in your local Maven repository: run `mvn install` in the RapidSwing
folder first.

```bash
mvn verify
java -jar target/{{artifactId}}-1.0.0-SNAPSHOT-app.jar
```

## Where things are

| File | What it does |
|---|---|
| `App.java` | Starts the application and builds its menus |
| `{{mainView}}.java` | The main window's content |
| `AppSupport.java` | Menus and features shared by the application |
| `src/main/resources/app.properties` | Title, theme and size of the window |
| `src/main/resources/messages*.properties` | All texts shown to the user |
| `AppSmokeTest.java` | A test that opens the main view, using `rapidswing-testing` |
{{#if rest}}
| `rest/` | Screens for the REST API, generated from its OpenAPI document |
{{/if}}
{{#if login}}

## Sign-in

The application has one account, `admin`. Its password was shown once when the project was generated; only a
hash is stored, in `AppSupport.java`. To set a new password, generate a hash:

```bash
java -cp rapidswing-core-{{rapidswingVersion}}.jar com.rapidswing.security.PasswordHasher
```

Signing in to a desktop client protects the user interface only. Protect the data itself on the server.
{{/if}}
{{#if rest}}

## REST API

The API's base URL is `api.url` in `app.properties`. The classes in `rest/` were generated from the API's
OpenAPI document and are yours to change.
{{/if}}
